{"duration_api_ms":13083,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8ecb3e00-88be-435b-9b72-379581e028a3","total_cost_usd":0.0015818,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":710,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2604,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2199},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":710,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2604,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":710,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":710},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1253,"outputTokens":2629,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":710,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0015818,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2199,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":710,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Application:** The ETF files a Section 6(c) exemptive application under the Investment Company Act, plus any other needed relief (e.g., Sections 12(d)(1), 17(a), 22(d)), usually after pre-filing discussions with SEC staff.\n\n**Notice:** Staff reviews the application and amendments. The SEC then issues a notice of application, published in the Federal Register, which opens a roughly 25-day window for interested persons to request a hearing.\n\n**Order:** If no hearing is requested and staff comments are resolved, the SEC issues the exemptive order. If a hearing is requested, the matter proceeds to a hearing process.\n\n**Expedited review:** Rule 0-5 allows an applicant to request expedited treatment, such as a shortened notice period. It is discretionary and generally requires a showing of urgency, with relief substantially identical to prior precedent.\n\n**45-day clock:** Under Rule 0-5, the Commission generally must act within 45 days of filing, meaning it issues a notice or takes other action on the application. This is a deadline on the Commission's initial step, not a total approval timeline. Overall time depends on staff comments, amendments, and any hearing.\n\nVerify current rule text before relying on this.","ttft_ms":10844,"type":"result","duration_ms":12395,"uuid":"d26eedb7-ff83-4e39-9cf7-ce2570bf276e","ttft_stream_ms":431,"time_to_request_ms":58,"first_content_frame_ms":431,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
